------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A. THE READER, CHECKED AGAINST YOSHIMURA'S OWN SAMPLED WIND
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1281 points along their path 1, every 10th step
  Their aircraft flies 090, so body x is east, body y SOUTH, body z
  down -- the expected signs are +1 on u and -1 on both v and w.

   ours   best match among their three columns        r as read
    u     -> their u  (r=+0.794, margin +0.207)   +0.7938   OK
    v     -> their v  (r=-0.866, margin +0.538)   -0.8659   OK
    w     -> their w  (r=-0.747, margin +0.444)   -0.7466   OK

  REGISTRATION, searched and reported but NOT applied:
    u: best r=+0.9747 at di=+2.00 dj=-0.25 dk=+1.25   their = +0.888*ours +0.68
    v: best r=-0.9553 at di=+1.25 dj=+0.25 dk=+1.25   their = -0.921*ours +5.26
    w: best r=-0.9736 at di=+1.00 dj=+0.00 dk=+1.50   their = -0.791*ours +0.09
    -> a 1-2 cell horizontal and ~1.3 level vertical residual, i.e.
       under 150 m. It is NOT fed back into the sampler: fitting an
       offset until the check passes would turn the only end-to-end
       check into a calibration. The run below uses ZERO offset.

  AND ONE REAL FINDING ABOUT THEIR SETUP. The u and v intercepts are
  -24.9 and +7.7 m/s while w's is +0.08: their recorded wind has the
  MEAN FLOW REMOVED, which w -- being zero-mean already -- does not
  show. So their columns are gust perturbations, not total wind.

